 "interpretation": "Descriptive robustness screen of one published discovery finding, using only the provided Overture building summary and the provided USFS WRC and MTBS strata fields. Resampling whole counties widens the interval relative to the published tract-level bootstrap because tracts inside a county share provider mix and reference vintage; the screen reports whether the documented high-burn versus unburned difference in the share of tracts whose Overture-to-USFS building-count ratio falls below the preregistered cutoff survives that dependence. It does not establish cause: fire does not provably change the mapping, and the ratio is a proxy for disagreement between two provided layers, not evidence that either layer is wrong and not evidence that any service or response differs. No organiser target, leaderboard value, removed reference layer or external source is used, and no county is excluded.",
